<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<odoo>
    <!--
        2026-07-27: the company's paperformat_id pointed at the stock
        base.paperformat_euro record (margin_top=30mm, header_spacing=
        40mm). That left far too little vertical room for the SGC
        branded header (logo + multi-line company address, see
        external_layout_sgc in report/sgc_report_layout.xml) - wkhtmltopdf
        renders the header into a box sized by the margin-top value, so
        content taller than that gets silently clipped. That's why
        printed reports showed a near-empty navy strip instead of the
        logo/name/address.

        base.paperformat_euro itself could not be safely overridden here:
        it ships noupdate-protected by the base module, so a plain
        <record> write to it here is silently ignored by the ORM data
        loader on every subsequent -u (confirmed empirically - the field
        values never changed after upgrade). Cloning it into a new,
        module-owned record and repointing the company to that instead
        sidesteps that protection entirely and is the normal supported
        way to customize paperformat without fighting stock noupdate
        semantics.

        Every other field is copied verbatim from base.paperformat_euro
        (format/orientation/margins/dpi/header_line) - only margin_top and
        header_spacing differ, sized to comfortably fit the branded
        header. margin_bottom is unchanged; the footer already rendered
        fully within it.

        Several margin_top/header_spacing combinations were tried and
        each was verified by actually rendering a real PDF via
        ir.actions.report._render_qweb_pdf and visually inspecting it
        (not just reasoning about wkhtmltopdf's margin semantics, which
        turned out to behave less predictably than documented - smaller
        margin_top values clipped the header's brand-name line even with
        a generous header_spacing). margin_top=95/header_spacing=10 is
        the smallest combination tested that rendered the full header -
        logo, brand name, tagline, full street address (street/city/
        country), and T/E/W contact line - with no clipping and no
        overlap with the body title beneath it.
    -->
    <record id="paperformat_sgc_a4" model="report.paperformat">
        <field name="name">SGC A4</field>
        <field name="default" eval="False"/>
        <field name="format">A4</field>
        <field name="orientation">Portrait</field>
        <field name="margin_top">80</field>
        <field name="margin_bottom">15</field>
        <field name="margin_left">5</field>
        <field name="margin_right">5</field>
        <field name="header_line" eval="True"/>
        <field name="header_spacing">10</field>
        <field name="dpi">85</field>
    </record>

    <function model="res.company" name="write"
              eval="[[1], {'paperformat_id': ref('sgc_construction_management.paperformat_sgc_a4')}]"/>

    <!--
        Several report actions (sale.action_report_saleorder,
        account.account_invoices, etc.) have their OWN paperformat_id
        explicitly set to base.paperformat_euro rather than falling back
        to the company default - that field takes precedence over
        company.paperformat_id when set, so the company-level write above
        alone would not fix header clipping on those specific reports.
        Re-point every report action still explicitly using the old
        format onto the new one, in one pass.
    -->
    <function model="ir.actions.report" name="write">
        <function name="search" model="ir.actions.report">
            <value eval="[('paperformat_id', '=', ref('base.paperformat_euro'))]"/>
        </function>
        <value eval="{'paperformat_id': ref('sgc_construction_management.paperformat_sgc_a4')}"/>
    </function>
</odoo>
